WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.330
Summer 2026.

2
00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:07.570
A survey asks people across the UK:
do you support renewable energy?

3
00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:09.890
79 per cent say yes.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:12.070
Just 4 per cent say no.

5
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:17.910
In 2025, fossil fuels still gave
86 per cent of the world's energy.

6
00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.490
But ask about a wind
farm near their own home,

7
00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.270
and the answer changes.

8
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.290
Do they think wind farms don't work?

9
00:00:24.340 --> 00:00:26.770
Or is something else going on?

10
00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:29.630
In this mission, you'll map who has a say,

11
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:33.030
from residents to energy
companies and governments.

12
00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:37.170
Then you'll use survey evidence to
explain the gap between support in general

13
00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.370
and support nearby.

14
00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.090
Your mission: explain why backing renewable
energy doesn't always mean backing

15
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:45.640
a wind farm nearby.
